{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794141208,"nonce":"Fm6BK6pRUsNxXknTgtsRo9EXm5I=","title":"Mobile apps ignore the system dark mode: scheme detection is a TODO on iOS and Android","message":"Found on the Android emulator while rebuilding the mobile example. With the system in night mode (cmd uimode night yes), a cold start of the example still renders the light scheme, and toggling night mode while it runs does not change it.\n\nCauses: blinc_theme::platform::android::detect_color_scheme and ::ios::detect_color_scheme return Light with a TODO (Configuration.uiMode, UITraitCollection). blinc_platform_ios::is_dark_mode also returns false with a TODO. blinc_platform_android::is_dark_mode(app) already reads Configuration.uiMode through JNI, but nothing calls it: the runners initialise the theme with detect_system_color_scheme(). Neither runner reacts to a later system change either.\n\nNeeded: detect the scheme at startup on both platforms (the Android runner has the AndroidApp handle; iOS needs UITraitCollection.userInterfaceStyle through objc2), and follow system changes at runtime (Android onConfigurationChanged / uiMode, iOS traitCollectionDidChange) by calling ThemeState::set_scheme. The theme-watcher feature exists for desktop and is not wired for mobile. Related: 4e110cb, af473a1.","files":null}]}